"schema-faq-answer\">Students, beginners, freshers, and working professionals from any stream are eligible for a web designing course. Most institutes accept candidates who have completed 10th or 12th from a recognized board.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1776161618403\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">2. Can I join a web designing course after 10th?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Yes, many certificate and diploma-level web designing courses allow students to join after completing 10th. These courses usually focus on basic design concepts, HTML, CSS, and website layout fundamentals.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1776161630199\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">3. Can I do a web designing course after 12th?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Yes, students can easily join certificate, diploma, and degree-level web designing courses after 12th. This is one of the most common eligibility requirements for advanced and career-focused programs.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1776161643696\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">4. Is coding knowledge required for a web designing course?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">No, prior coding knowledge is generally not required for a web designing course. Most beginner-friendly courses start with the basics of HTML, CSS, design tools, and responsive website design.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1776161657112\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">5. What are the minimum marks required for a web designing course?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Most certificate and diploma courses do not have strict percentage requirements. Degree-level courses may require around 45% to 50% marks in the previous qualifying examination depending on the institute.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1776161668956\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">6. Is there any age limit for joining a web designing course?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">No, there is usually no fixed age limit for joining a web designing course. Students, freshers, career switchers, and working professionals of different age groups can easily enroll.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1776161680750\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">7. Can beginners apply for a web designing course?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Yes, beginners can easily apply for a web designing course. Most courses are designed to start from basic concepts, making them suitable for learners with no prior experience.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1776161694592\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">8. Can working professionals join a web designing course?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Yes, working professionals can join web designing courses to upskill, switch careers, or start freelancing. Online and weekend courses make it easier to learn alongside a job.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1776161705800\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">9. What is the eligibility for an online web designing course?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Online web designing courses usually have simple eligibility criteria. Anyone with basic computer knowledge and an interest in learning website design can join, even without strict academic requirements.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1776161715388\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">10. What is the eligibility for a diploma in web designing?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">For a diploma in web designing, most institutes require candidates to have completed 10th or 12th from a recognized board, usually with around 40% to 50% marks.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1776161727947\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">11. What is the eligibility for a degree course in web designing?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Degree-level web designing courses generally require candidates to complete 12th from a recognized board with around 45% to 50% marks, depending on the college or university.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1776161741527\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">12. How long does a web designing course take?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">The duration depends on the course type. Certificate courses may take 1\u20133 months, diploma courses 6\u201312 months, and degree courses usually take 3\u20134 years.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1776161753017\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">13. What are the fees for a web designing course?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Web designing course fees vary by course type and institute. Online courses may start from \u20b910,000, while diploma and degree courses can range from \u20b930,000 to \u20b93,00,000+.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1776161765382\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">14. Can I get a job after completing a web designing course?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Yes, after completing a web designing course, you can apply for roles such as web designer, UI\/UX designer, front-end developer, freelancer, or website consultant across different industries.<\/p> <\/div> <\/div>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Conclusion<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Choosing the right course starts with understanding the eligibility criteria for web designing courses, including qualifications, required skills, and basic requirements. This helps students, beginners, and working professionals select the most suitable certificate, diploma, or degree program.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>With flexible learning options and strong career opportunities, web designing is an excellent field to build creative and technical skills. 